D3D12: a depth-stencil view passed as RenderingDesc::depth alone has its stencil cleared too.

NRIDescs.h says "depth" may be treated as depth-stencil, and both backends treat such a view's
stencil as attached: Vulkan points pStencilAttachment at the depth attachment when the format has
stencil, D3D12 sets m_Stencil = m_Depth. But D3D12's BeginRendering takes the stencil clear flag and
value from RenderingDesc::stencil only, so the stencil is loaded, not cleared, while Vulkan clears it
with the depth attachment's load op and clear value. Since 110a667.

This clears the stencil when there is a stencil attachment and the attachment that provides it
(RenderingDesc::stencil if given, else RenderingDesc::depth) asks for CLEAR, with that attachment's
clear value.
Measured on v190, NVIDIA and WARP: over a stencil of 9, a pass with the view as depth only, LoadOp
CLEAR and a stencil clear value of 5 left 5 on Vulkan and 9 on D3D12 (an EQUAL 5 draw drew nothing,
an EQUAL 9 draw drew). With the change D3D12 leaves 5, as Vulkan does (NVIDIA).

diff --git a/Source/D3D12/CommandBufferD3D12.hpp b/Source/D3D12/CommandBufferD3D12.hpp
index 7a09498..986537a 100644
--- a/Source/D3D12/CommandBufferD3D12.hpp
+++ b/Source/D3D12/CommandBufferD3D12.hpp
@@ -1831,14 +1831,16 @@ NRI_INLINE void CommandBufferD3D12::BeginRendering(const RenderingDesc& renderin
             GetGraphicsCommandList()->ClearRenderTargetView(renderTargets[i], &attachmentDesc.clearValue.color.f.x, 0, nullptr);
     }
 
+    const AttachmentDesc& stencil = renderingDesc.stencil.descriptor ? renderingDesc.stencil : renderingDesc.depth; // "depth" may be treated as depth-stencil
+
     D3D12_CLEAR_FLAGS clearFlags = (D3D12_CLEAR_FLAGS)0;
     if (renderingDesc.depth.loadOp == LoadOp::CLEAR)
         clearFlags |= D3D12_CLEAR_FLAG_DEPTH;
-    if (renderingDesc.stencil.loadOp == LoadOp::CLEAR)
+    if (m_Stencil.attachment && stencil.loadOp == LoadOp::CLEAR)
         clearFlags |= D3D12_CLEAR_FLAG_STENCIL;
 
     if (clearFlags)
-        GetGraphicsCommandList()->ClearDepthStencilView(depthStencil, clearFlags, renderingDesc.depth.clearValue.depthStencil.depth, renderingDesc.stencil.clearValue.depthStencil.stencil, 0, nullptr);
+        GetGraphicsCommandList()->ClearDepthStencilView(depthStencil, clearFlags, renderingDesc.depth.clearValue.depthStencil.depth, stencil.clearValue.depthStencil.stencil, 0, nullptr);
 
     // Shading rate
     if (m_Device.GetDesc().tiers.shadingRate >= 2) {
